## 1. Plan what is shared

Teamwork in NAHPU relies on every device holding *identical* copies of shared
records (i.e., with the same UUIDs). When catalogs are merged, NAHPU recognizes
those UUIDs and matches the records instead of duplicating them. Records that
only one person uses (e.g., the site and event for their own line in Workflow
B) stay on that person's device until the merge, which brings them in as new.

| Record | Created by | How teammates receive it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Project identity | Heru | Project QR (or project-info JSON) |
| Personnel, including all catalogers | Heru | Carried inside site and event transfers |
| Sites `TJHH-L1` and `TJHH-P1` (Workflow A) | Heru | Site QR (or site JSON) |
| Events for both sites (Workflow A) | Heru | Event JSON file |
| Site `TJBS-L2` and its event (Workflow B) | Bima | Merged at the end |
| Taxa for Bima's specimens | Heru | Taxon QR (or exact name entry) |
| Specimen records | Each cataloger | Merged at the end |
| Field journal | Each cataloger | Kept per device (not merged) |

## 2. Heru: set up the shared context

On **Heru's device**, follow Basic tutorials 2–4 using the values below.

{% steps %}

1. Create the project with `Mammalogy` as the main taxon format and **personnel
   Field ID** mode:

    | Field | Value |
    | --- | --- |
    | Project name | `Tujuh teamwork 2014` |
    | Description | `Two-cataloger practice project (Workflows A and B) built from the 2014 Mt. Tujuh small-mammal survey, Kerinci, Jambi.` |
    | Time zone | `Asia/Jakarta` |

    Project names accept letters, numbers, spaces, hyphens, and underscores, up
    to 25 characters. A period, as in `Mt.`, is not accepted.

2. Add personnel. Heru creates **all** team members here, including Bima:

    | `Name*` | Role | `Initials` | `Cataloger number*` |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | `Heru Handika` | `Cataloger` | `HH` | `445` |
    | `Bima Sampel` | `Cataloger` | `BS` | `1` |
    | `Citra Contoh` | `None` | `CC` | Leave empty |

3. Register five taxa in `Taxon registry`: *Mus crociduroides*, *Maxomys
   hylomyoides*, and *Niviventer cremoriventer* (Rodentia, Muridae);
   *Crocidura neglecta* and *Crocidura beccarii* (Eulipotyphla, Soricidae).

4. Create the sites `TJHH-L1` (`Trapline`) and `TJHH-P1` (`Pitfall line`) with
   the geography, habitat, and `TJHH-PM` coordinate from
   [Basic tutorial 3](/en/tutorials/basic/sites/).

5. Create one collecting event per site, 12–16 September 2014, with the methods
   and notes from [Basic tutorial 4](/en/tutorials/basic/events/): 31 snap
   traps on `TJHH-L1` and 10 pitfalls on `TJHH-P1`. Add Heru Handika as
   `Leader`, and Bima Sampel and Citra Contoh as `Helper`, on both events.

{% /steps %}

{% aside type="caution" title="Why we recommend sharing personnel across devices" %}
Bima can create his own personnel record on his device if needed, but we
recommend creating each person once and sharing personnel across devices so
their UUID stays the same everywhere. NAHPU identifies each person by a UUID,
not by name, so creating the same person independently on two devices causes
the merge to treat them as two different people named Bima Sampel. Created once
on Heru's device, Bima's record travels to Bima's device inside the event
transfer with the same UUID. Because the `Cataloger` role cannot be changed
after a person is created, set it now.
{% /aside %}

